DEVICE SPIKE

# Robot Lab: the excavator digs, swings a quarter turn, dumps, and swings back.
# Model: Excavator. Wheels on A and B, the turntable on C (an 8-tooth gear on the
# 28-tooth turntable: 315 degrees of the motor turn it 90 degrees), and three linear
# actuators: D lifts the boom, E swings the stick, F curls the bucket.
# The motors turn the actuators' spindles one to one: 360 degrees push 1.2 mm.
WHEN flag clicked:
  set motor stop action A hold
  set motor stop action B hold
  set motor stop action C hold
  set motor stop action D hold
  set motor stop action E hold
  set motor stop action F hold
  run motor A clockwise 1 degrees
  run motor B clockwise 1 degrees
  set motor speed C 10
  set motor speed D 100
  set motor speed E 100
  set motor speed F 100
  # Dig: open the bucket and lift the boom a little while the stick reaches out (the
  # three move together: broadcasts start the shorter moves, the longest is waited for),
  # lower the boom until the teeth touch the ground, then curl the bucket in while the
  # boom comes up a little.
  broadcast "open bucket"
  broadcast "raise boom"
  run motor E counterclockwise 3000 degrees
  run motor D counterclockwise 5000 degrees
  broadcast "boom up a little"
  run motor F clockwise 5000 degrees
  # Lift the load: boom up while the stick comes in.
  broadcast "stick in"
  run motor D clockwise 5000 degrees
  # Swing left a quarter turn and dump.
  run motor C clockwise 315 degrees
  run motor F counterclockwise 5000 degrees
  # Swing back, then a quarter turn the other way and home again.
  run motor C counterclockwise 630 degrees
  run motor C clockwise 315 degrees

WHEN I receive "open bucket":
  run motor F counterclockwise 2500 degrees

WHEN I receive "raise boom":
  run motor D clockwise 1000 degrees

WHEN I receive "boom up a little":
  run motor D clockwise 2500 degrees

WHEN I receive "stick in":
  run motor E clockwise 3000 degrees
